  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Symposium - 2020 U.S.-India Aviation Partnership Summit, through American Association of Airport Executives</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The 2020 India Aviation Partnership Summit in the United States will include an up to two-day symposium; one day of site visits with U.S. companies and/or airport facilities in the local area, and a meeting of the U.S. - India Aviation Cooperation Program (ACP). The seventh biennial Aviation Summit will convene a high-level dialogue, featuring U.S. technical and regulatory expertise that can support India&apos;s rapidly growing aviation markets while addressing key issues related to aviation safety and security; standards harmonization; air traffic management and control; procurement practices, and airspace utilization. This funding in the amount of $23,989 is being added to the India Aviation Partnership Summit, bringing the new total amount to $493,312. This funding in the amount of $35,000 is being added to the India Aviation Partnership Summit to cover the travel costs for the attendance of up to ten additional South Asian aviation representatives.</narrative>
  </description>
